      "writtenOn": "2012-03-05T21:54:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this null-termination part of the SMBus bytestream protocol, or is it there because we\u0027re only currently using this to read ASCII strings?\n\nEither way, it\u0027d be good to note this in the declaration in i2c.h (that if you want to read a block of N bytes of binary data, you\u0027d better pass a len\u003eN buffer)",
